These commands expose the Windows routing table, VMware virtual adapters, wireless network configuration, VPN adapter, subnet masks, and default gateways.
6.4 Cisco troubleshooting commands
show ip interface brief
show ip route
show ip route connected
show interfaces GigabitEthernet0/0
show arp
The connected route installed by V1 was compared against the physical wireless network's address range.
6.5 Resolution
Rather than attempting to continue troubleshooting the VPN with overlapping networks, the CML external connectivity design was changed.
The CML internal NAT connection was replaced with a System Bridge connection, allowing V1 to obtain an address from the VMware NAT network.
This separated the virtual router's underlay subnet from the physical wireless subnet.
