15.2 Explanation of each command
crypto ikev2 proposal CML-PROPOSAL
Creates a named collection of cryptographic algorithms used during IKEv2 negotiation.
encryption aes-cbc-256
Specifies AES encryption with a 256-bit key for the IKE security association.
integrity sha256
Specifies SHA-256-based integrity protection.
prf sha256
Specifies the pseudorandom function used during key derivation.
group 19
Specifies a 256-bit elliptic-curve Diffie-Hellman group.
The IKEv2 proposal determines how the peers establish a protected control-plane relationship.
